  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Climate Finance- Contribution to Central African Forest Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Central African Forest Initiative (CAFI) is a multi-donor partnership that supports Central African countries in their efforts to combat deforestation and forest degradation while promoting sustainable economic development. Through its results framework and support to national REDD+ strategies, CAFI finances reforms and investments aimed at sustainable land management, the conservation of the Congo Basin forests, and the reduction of emissions associated with land-use change. Canopy Trust seeks to finance projects and businesses that reduce deforestation and promote sustainable land-use practices in Central Africa. The project is aligned with national REDD+ strategies and the CAFI results framework through targeted interventions in sustainable agriculture, agroforestry, and forest conservation. It is implemented by the Swiss foundation Catalytic Finance, which specializes in the structuring of blended finance mechanisms. Canopy Trust is expected to expand the range of investment instruments and financing solutions available to the partnership, which is currently largely limited to grant funding. The project supports the region&#x2019;s sustainable development objectives by contributing to reduced deforestation while fostering economic growth through sustainable practices in the agriculture, forestry, and infrastructure sectors</narrative>
  </description>
